> Bridge implementation inputs

Implement the public AF_UNIX/SOCK_DGRAM PacketFlowBridge EXACTLY per the TASK-260715-p89bdj contract (authoritative: descriptor/task ownership, forward+reverse 4-byte network-order AF framing with SDK constants, the full EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK->would-block-drop, ENOBUFS->drop-no-retry, EMSGSIZE/EOF/persistent->single-fatal error table, bounded count/time work slices + 4+MTU ceiling, no application queue, no unbounded side buffer). USE the TASK-260720-9xy8yx PacketFlowAdapterBoundary for the read lifecycle (do NOT reimplement continuation/cancellation handling). Endpoint A stays bridge-owned; endpoint B is a scoped exclusive borrow handed to HEV and closed only after HEV blocking main returns (per uopycx facts). Both endpoints: preserve flags + add CLOEXEC/NONBLOCK, raise SO_SNDBUF/SO_RCVBUF, expose requested/effective gauges. Prohibit utun control access, FD scanning/reopening/duplication, unbounded retries. Deterministic Swift Testing for start/stop/cancel/startup-fail/runtime-fail (join children + HEV borrow before closing B then A exactly once), forward/reverse framing, all error transitions + counters, metric names/units/monotonicity/maxima, first-error-wins, privacy-safe logs. Build+test via swift build/test on macOS in the harness; HEV side may be a test double.




## Board CLI Reference

You have access to `task-board` CLI for managing your work. All writes use the `m` (mutation DSL) subcommand:

```bash
