The compiler is spending minutes at 100% CPU type-checking the readiness implementation, which points to a Swift constraint-solver blowup rather than a runtime/tool deadlock. I’m interrupting this pass and simplifying the generic continuation/C-pointer expressions before rerunning; that keeps build latency sane and makes the seam easier to audit.
